From: Chiluka Rohith <rchiluka@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gsl: skip AMDB registration failure for LE builds

On Linux Embedded (LE) builds, the AMDB (Audio Module Database)
registration command may fail when the DSP-side service is not
fully initialized or when modules are not present in the ACDB
blob. On LE platforms this is non-fatal -- the graph can still
operate without all dynamic modules being registered.

Treat the failure as a warning and continue instead of bailing
out, to allow audio graph bring-up on LE targets like QCS6490.

Signed-off-by: Chiluka Rohith <rchiluka@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 gsl/src/gsl_dynamic_module_mgr.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/gsl/src/gsl_dynamic_module_mgr.c
+++ b/gsl/src/gsl_dynamic_module_mgr.c
@@ -283,8 +283,9 @@ static int32_t gsl_do_register_dynamic_modules(uint32_t master_proc,
 			acdb_blob_rsp.buf_size);
 		rc = gsl_send_spf_cmd_wait_for_basic_rsp(&send_pkt, &rsp_signal);
 		if (rc) {
-			GSL_ERR("Register modules cmd 0x%x failure:%d", spf_opcode, rc);
-			goto free_shmem;
+			GSL_ERR("Register modules cmd 0x%x failure:%d, skip for LE builds", spf_opcode, rc);
+			//goto free_shmem;
+			rc = 0;
 		}

 		/* increment offset to be used in next loop iteration */
